    {
      "id": "p0228-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby noted that the phrase \"King Dad\" is a reference to the Super Mario Bros. television cartoons that first aired in the late 1980s and early 1990s. Specifically, the phrase is from the Adventures of Super Mario Bros. 3 series, in which the villain's children regularly call their father \"King Dad\".",
        "raw": "Toby noted that the phrase \"King Dad\" is a reference to the Super Mario Bros.\ntelevision cartoons that first aired in the late 1980s and early 1990s. Specifically,\nthe phrase is from the Adventures of Super Mario Bros. 3 series, in which the\nvillain's children regularly call their father \"King Dad\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29710454,
          0.73365714,
          0.911799,
          0.80044286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2932118,
          0.73294286,
          0.91384243,
          0.80151429
